===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|eo|de|Punkt}}, {{bor|eo|ru|пункт}}, {{bor|eo|pl|punkt}}, all from {{der|eo|la|pūnctum||point; puncture}}, from {{m|la|pūnctus||pierced, punctured; marked with points, stippled}}, from {{m|la|pungō||I prick, puncture}}. Compare {{cog|ro|punct}}, {{cog|sv|punkt}}, as well as the second half of {{m+|en|interpunct}}. {{doublet|eo|bunta|poento}}.

